From 942c749c634fd6e89a84e7fb762cc53f878b8262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 19:49:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add the three remaining minor design-time helpers

Closes the last non-non-goal type gaps: DataGridViewColumnDesignTimeVisibleAttribute
(with Yes/No/Default and Visible), DataGridViewCellStyleConverter (a TypeConverter
advertising InstanceDescriptor), and ToolStripDropDownItemAccessibleObject
(exposing the owning item's MenuItem role and text). WinForms derives the last
from ToolStripItem.ToolStripItemAccessibleObject, which the shim does not project,
so it derives directly from AccessibleObject - a cosmetic base difference the
surface diff does not see.

After this, every net48 missing type is a declared non-goal. Covered by
DesignTimeHelpersFunctionalTests. Full Forms suite green at 2504.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
